Translation patch: `ComStmtExecuteRequest::params` stored as a slice

Change: The field `params: Vec<&'a Value>` becomes `params: &'a [Value]`. `build` stores the input slice instead of `params.iter().collect::<Vec<_>>()`. The accessor `params()` returns `&'a [Value]` (it was `&[&'a Value]`). `serialize` reads `&self.params[i]`.
Why: Aeneas does not support a borrow nested in a borrow through a generic instantiation. Every access to a `Vec<&Value>` through `&self` (`len`, indexing, iteration) is a `&Vec<&Value>`, and fails with "Nested borrows are not supported yet" or "Internal error ... Found an already registered mapping".
Behaviour: Identical for serialization and for every use inside the crate: element `i` is the same `Value` in both, since the vector held `&params[i]` at position `i`. The derived `Debug`, `PartialEq` and `Clone` of the request are element-wise the same. API difference: `params()` returns a slice of values instead of a slice of references to them. The crate does not call it.

